  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880256",
      "title": "Working with Watchers",
      "lectureOrder": 294,
      "videoOrder": 261,
      "sourceHash": "ae8af92620452e8b92e52a2681529b4f95565ca65c205a46a8d248ca134741c6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.84,
          "en": "So, now let's have a look at the last option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.84,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "we want to replace, and that's the watch option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.1,
          "en": "Watch can be useful for running some code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.1,
          "end": 15.2,
          "en": "like setting up behind the scenes HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.2,
          "end": 17.083,
          "en": "when some data changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.35,
          "end": 21.13,
          "en": "Of course, I don't want to send that HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.13,
          "end": 22.15,
          "en": "in the simple app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.15,
          "end": 25.4,
          "en": "but I still want to show you a how watch works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.4,
          "end": 30.4,
          "en": "Normally, you add your watch option here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.65,
          "end": 32.41,
          "en": "which watch is object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.41,
          "end": 34.84,
          "en": "and in there, you could then watch age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.84,
          "end": 36.89,
          "en": "by adding a method of the same name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.89,
          "end": 40.03,
          "en": "so watch this age property by adding such a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.03,
          "end": 43.99,
          "en": "you would get the new value whenever watch triggers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.99,
          "end": 48.83,
          "en": "and then you could console log val here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.83,
          "end": 50.963,
          "en": "That's what you could do with watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.57,
          "end": 55.04,
          "en": "Well, obviously that's not what we're doing now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.04,
          "end": 60.04,
          "en": "instead we import a new thing from view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.43,
          "end": 64.82300000000001,
          "en": "and that thing is another function, the watch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 70.1,
          "en": "The watch function is all the part of the Composition API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.1,
          "end": 72.9,
          "en": "and the watch function allows us to register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.9,
          "end": 76.3,
          "en": "a watcher inside of this setup method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.3,
          "end": 79.48,
          "en": "And yes, it's quite normal that you have a lot of things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.48,
          "end": 82.97,
          "en": "in this setup method, as you can tell already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.97,
          "end": 87.34,
          "en": "So in here, let's say here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.34,
          "end": 91.81,
          "en": "after we defined our refs, we can call watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.81,
          "end": 95.2,
          "en": "Now, watch wants two arguments here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.2,
          "end": 100.2,
          "en": "the first argument, is a dependency of watch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.42,
          "end": 105.19,
          "en": "telling watch when it should execute the watcher function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.19,
          "end": 109.02000000000001,
          "en": "and for example, here we could pass the uAge ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.02000000000001,
          "end": 112.75,
          "en": "So this ref is now a dependency of watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.75,
          "end": 115.81,
          "en": "The second argument is the actual function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.81,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "that should be called then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 120.46,
          "en": "Now, we need to specify this dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.46,
          "end": 122.66,
          "en": "because with the Options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.66,
          "end": 126.84,
          "en": "the dependency was just the name of the watch method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 126.84,
          "end": 129.64,
          "en": "Now, it's just watch as a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.64,
          "end": 131.83,
          "en": "so to still let watch know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.83,
          "end": 134.2,
          "en": "when the watcher function should run,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.2,
          "end": 137.63,
          "en": "we need to specify the pendency first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.63,
          "end": 139.12,
          "en": "So, that's uAge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.12,
          "end": 143.083,
          "en": "and then whenever uAge changes, this function is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.6,
          "end": 145.5,
          "en": "In this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.5,
          "end": 149.44,
          "en": "we now actually get two arguments automatically by watch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.44,
          "end": 153.49,
          "en": "and that's the new value and the old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.49,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "So, we get to the value of uAge before it changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 159.19299999999998,
          "en": "and then after the change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.47,
          "end": 165.47,
          "en": "And here we can console log old age plus old value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.24,
          "end": 170.82999999999998,
          "en": "and then also console log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.79,
          "end": 177.123,
          "en": "new age plus new value, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.31,
          "end": 180.29,
          "en": "And that's all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 180.29,
          "end": 183.94,
          "en": "If we now save this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.94,
          "end": 186.57,
          "en": "nothing is printed here, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.57,
          "end": 190.25,
          "en": "But if I now click change age, which changes the age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.25,
          "end": 193.01,
          "en": "we see old age, 31,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.01,
          "end": 194.73,
          "en": "new age, 33,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.73,
          "end": 198.84,
          "en": "because our watch are executed since we changed age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.84,
          "end": 200.493,
          "en": "which is our dependency here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 202.04,
          "end": 206.11,
          "en": "Actually, you can also specify more than one dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.11,
          "end": 209.86,
          "en": "so that you even gain more flexibility than with watch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.86,
          "end": 214.023,
          "en": "the Options API, by passing an array of dependencies here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 215.44,
          "end": 218.11,
          "en": "Then here, you could specify uAge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 219.26,
          "end": 223.76,
          "en": "and let's say uName as a dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 223.76,
          "end": 226.87,
          "en": "and therefore, let's move watch below uName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 226.87,
          "end": 228.903,
          "en": "so that we do have access to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.77,
          "end": 234.15,
          "en": "So now, either when age or does computed ref changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 234.15,
          "end": 237.6,
          "en": "when either of these two changes, this function executes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.6,
          "end": 239.32,
          "en": "and then we actually also get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 239.32,
          "end": 242.89,
          "en": "different kinds of values here, as arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.89,
          "end": 247.67,
          "en": "We get our new values here and our old values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 247.67,
          "end": 250.18,
          "en": "We now get a raise for both arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 250.18,
          "end": 252.23,
          "en": "because we have more than one dependency.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 253.34,
          "end": 257.38,
          "en": "So our old age now is old values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 257.38,
          "end": 259.2,
          "en": "and then the first element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 259.2,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "since the age is our first dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 262.17,
          "end": 266.4,
          "en": "and our new age is new values, and then the first element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 266.4,
          "end": 268.78,
          "en": "Because if you have more than one dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.78,
          "end": 272.09000000000003,
          "en": "you get more than one value for these arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 272.09000000000003,
          "end": 273.93,
          "en": "and the order of values here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 273.93,
          "end": 276.173,
          "en": "follows the order of your dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.3,
          "end": 279.68,
          "en": "Hence, of course, if you want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 279.68,
          "end": 282.68,
          "en": "we can also copy those console log statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 282.68,
          "end": 286.13,
          "en": "and output the old name, which has old values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 286.13,
          "end": 288.49,
          "en": "and then the second element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 288.49,
          "end": 291.62,
          "en": "and new name, which is new values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 291.62,
          "end": 293.163,
          "en": "and then the second element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 295.565,
          "end": 299.3,
          "en": "Now with that saved, if we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 299.3,
          "end": 300.97,
          "en": "I can change the age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 300.97,
          "end": 302.96,
          "en": "and you'll see old age, new age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 302.96,
          "end": 305.15,
          "en": "and nothing for old name and new name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.15,
          "end": 307.57,
          "en": "because there we didn't enter anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 307.57,
          "end": 311.15,
          "en": "But if I now start typing here, maybe just one character,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 311.15,
          "end": 313.1,
          "en": "we see the watcher fires again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.1,
          "end": 316.41,
          "en": "because now the age didn't change, but the name did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 316.41,
          "end": 320.61,
          "en": "So, you even gain more flexibility with this watch function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.61,
          "end": 324.49,
          "en": "because now, unlike in the Options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 324.49,
          "end": 328.77,
          "en": "where you always had just one dependency per watcher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 328.77,
          "end": 331.5,
          "en": "you can now have multiple dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 331.5,
          "end": 334.23,
          "en": "that trigger this watcher function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 334.23,
          "end": 336.36,
          "en": "And that's how you replace watch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 336.36,
          "end": 340.33299999999997,
          "en": "with this watch function when using the Composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
